:: Conditioning Lesson 1
<<if $mmagymintro is 1 and $phase is 0>><<pass 15>><</if>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "mma_gym">><<effects>>

<<if $mmagymintro isnot 1>>
	<<mmagymintro "Conditioning Lesson 1">>
<<else>>
    <<tiredness 6>><<wearandtear>><<npc Riley>><<person1>>
    <<cleareventpool>>
    <<addinlineevent "Tire Flips">>
        The gym air is thick with sweat and rubber as Riley leads you to the far side of the floor. A massive tractor tire, its surface worn and cracked from years of abuse, sits there like an immovable challenge.
        <br><br>

        "Alright, you've got 15 minutes. Ten flips, no excuses. Get moving." Riley's voice is sharp, with zero patience for hesitation.
        <br><br>

        You drop into a squat, fingers digging under the tire's heavy, grooved surface. 
        <<if $physique gte 10000>><<physique 1>><<set _effort to 0>>
            The weight is barely a factor. With a solid grip and a sharp drive from your legs, the tire lifts like it's part of your routine. Each flip is smooth, controlled, and efficient. Riley watches but doesn't comment—just gives the smallest nod of approval.
        <<elseif $physique gte 6000>><<physique 2>><<set _effort to 1>>
            It's heavy, but manageable. Your muscles engage, pushing through resistance, but your form stays solid. The tire crashes down after the first flip, and you roll your shoulders, getting into the rhythm. Riley watches with a neutral expression.
        <<elseif $physique gte 3000>><<physique 3>><<set _effort to 2>>
            The tire fights you every inch of the way. Your grip tightens, legs shaking under the strain as you force it up. When it finally tips over with a dull THUD, Riley exhales sharply. "Gonna take all day?"
        <<else>><<physique 4>><<set _effort to 3>>
            You heave, but the tire barely budges. A second attempt gets it a few inches off the ground before it slams back down. Sweat stings your eyes as Riley shakes their head. "Pathetic. Try again."
        <</if>>
        <br><br>

        Riley doesn't let up. "Don't slow down, pick up the damn pace."
        <<if _effort is 0 or $willpower gte 600>><<willpower 0.25>>
            Your breathing stays controlled, each flip a steady, efficient motion. The weight no longer feels like a challenge—just another rep. Riley crosses their arms. "Good. Keep that up, and maybe you'll last in a real fight."
        <<elseif _effort is 1 or $willpower gte 400>><<willpower 0.5>>
            Your arms burn, but you grit your teeth and push through. By the seventh rep, sweat drips freely, but you keep moving. Riley gives a smirk. "Feeling it? Good. That's how you grow."
        <<elseif _effort is 2 or $willpower gte 200>><<willpower 1>>
            By the sixth flip, your breath is ragged. Your grip is slipping, and the tire gets heavier with each attempt. The last few reps feel like dragging dead weight. Riley grunts. "This is where most people quit. You gonna prove me wrong?"
        <<else>><<willpower 2>>
            Your body is screaming to stop. By the eighth rep, your legs shake, and you barely have the strength to flip it over. The last two flips take everything you have, leaving you hunched over, gasping. Riley lets out a long sigh. "Not good enough. You want to survive out there? Fix that."
        <</if>>
        <br><br>

        Riley cracks their knuckles. "That's 15 minutes down. Next station. Don't waste my time."
    <</addinlineevent>>
    <<addinlineevent "Farmer's Walk">>
        The gym floor feels solid under your feet, but this drill isn't about standing still—it's about moving with weight.
        <br><br>

        Riley stands beside a pair of heavy kettlebells, their handles wrapped in layers of worn grip tape. "Simple drill. Pick 'em up, walk to the other side, turn around, and do it again. No setting them down, no stopping. 15 minutes. Go."
        <br><br>

        You crouch down, gripping the cold metal handles, feeling their weight settle into your hands.
        <<if $physique gte 10000>><<physique 1>><<set _effort to 0>>
            The weight is solid, but nowhere near your limit. You stand up smoothly, grip firm, shoulders engaged. Each step is precise, controlled, and effortless.
            <br><br>
            Riley watches with a neutral expression, then gives the slightest nod. "Good. Keep that form. Don't get sloppy."
        <<elseif $physique gte 6000>><<physique 2>><<set _effort to 1>>
            The weight hits, but you handle it well. Your arms tense, forearms burning slightly, but you keep your pace steady. Each step reinforces your grip, and you focus on endurance.
            <br><br>
            Riley watches you work, offering no praise—just observation.
        <<elseif $physique gte 3000>><<physique 3>><<set _effort to 2>>
            The strain is immediate. Your grip tightens painfully as the kettlebells pull at your arms. Each step feels heavier, shoulders aching. You're fighting against the weight rather than controlling it.
            <br><br>
            Riley exhales sharply. "This gonna be a walk or a damn struggle? Get it together."
        <<else>><<physique 4>><<set _effort to 3>>
            The kettlebells nearly rip your arms out of their sockets. Your grip is weak, your steps unsteady, and every movement is a fight not to drop them immediately. The weights sway dangerously, pulling you off balance.
            <br><br>
            Riley shakes their head. "You drop 'em, you start over. You better figure this out fast."
        <</if>>
        <br><br>

        As the minutes drag on, the real challenge kicks in—endurance, control, and sheer mental willpower.
        <br><br>

        Riley doesn't let up. "No stopping. No resting. Keep moving."
        <<if _effort is 0 or $willpower gte 600>><<willpower 0.25>>
            Your grip holds strong, your pace steady, your mind locked in. The fatigue tries to creep in, but you shut it out. This is just another rep. Another drill. Nothing more.
            <br><br>
            Riley grunts in approval. "You might actually have some grit. Don't waste it."
        <<elseif _effort is 1 or $willpower gte 400>><<willpower 0.5>>
            Your arms burn, fingers barely holding on, but you refuse to quit. Every step is a battle, but you grind through it, forcing yourself forward.
            <br><br>
            Riley smirks. "Barely holding on? Good. That's when it starts working."
        <<elseif _effort is 2 or $willpower gte 200>><<willpower 1>>
            Your fingers are numb, shoulders screaming. Every second feels longer. By the final stretch, you're stumbling, legs shaky, grip on the verge of giving out.
            <br><br>
            Riley watches, unimpressed. "This is where most people break. You gonna prove me wrong?"
        <<else>><<willpower 2>>
            Your grip fails first. The kettlebells slip from your hands, crashing onto the floor before you even reach the turnaround point. You flex your fingers, but they're dead weight. You can't even lift them again right away.
            <br><br>
            Riley exhales through their nose. "Weak grip, weak resolve."
        <</if>>
        <br><br>

        Riley cracks their knuckles. "That's 15 minutes down. Next station. Don't waste my time."
    <</addinlineevent>>
    <<addinlineevent "Sledgehammer Swings">>
        The gym's back area is built for raw, brutal training. No machines, no fancy gear, just iron, sweat, and pain. In the corner, a massive tractor tire sits waiting, its rubber surface already battered from countless strikes.
        <br><br>

        Riley hands you a sledgehammer, its handle worn from years of punishment. The weight feels real in your grip.
        <br><br>

        "Fifty swings. Full power. No half-assed taps. If you're too slow, you start over." Riley's expression is stone-cold.
        <br><br>

        You set your stance, grip firm, shoulders squared. Time to work.
        <<if $physique gte 10000>><<physique 1>><<set _effort to 0>>
            The hammer moves like an extension of your body. Each swing is fluid and powerful, the head smashing into the tire with a deep, resounding thud. The impact barely slows you down, and your muscles don't even feel the strain yet.
            <br><br>
            Riley watches, unimpressed but not correcting you. "Good power. Keep that pace."
        <<elseif $physique gte 6000>><<physique 2>><<set _effort to 1>>
            Each swing sends shockwaves through your arms, but you stay steady. The burn starts early, but you push through, muscles engaging with every downward arc. The hammer lands clean, the tire absorbing every impact.
            <br><br>
            Riley grunts. "Not bad. Don't slow down."
        <<elseif $physique gte 3000>><<physique 3>><<set _effort to 2>>
            The first few swings feel fine, then the fatigue kicks in. Your grip slips slightly as the hammer starts to feel heavier with every rep. Your arms burn, but you keep swinging, muscles locking up from the strain.
            <br><br>
            Riley exhales sharply. "If you are already feeling it, you are not gonna last long."
        <<else>><<physique 4>><<set _effort to 3>>
            The hammer feels like dead weight in your hands. You barely lift it overhead, and when you bring it down, it bounces weakly off the tire instead of landing with force. Your grip is unstable, your swings uncoordinated.
            <br><br>
            Riley pinches the bridge of their nose. "This ain't some toy. Swing it like you mean it. Don't waste my time."
        <</if>>
        <br><br>

        The real test begins as the reps climb.
        <br><br>

        Riley does not let up. "Keep swinging. Don't break rhythm."
        <<if _effort is 0 or $willpower gte 600>><<willpower 0.25>>
            Your body moves on instinct. The burn is there, but you shut it out, just hammer, swing, impact, repeat. The rhythm stays perfect, every hit as powerful as the first.
            <br><br>
            Riley finally gives a small nod. "Yeah. That's how you do it."
        <<elseif _effort is 1 or $willpower gte 400>><<willpower 0.5>>
            Your arms are screaming, but your mind refuses to stop. Each swing takes more effort, but you force it through. You are slowing slightly, but you refuse to break form.
            <br><br>
            Riley smirks. "That's the pain setting in. Good. Now push past it."
        <<elseif _effort is 2 or $willpower gte 200>><<willpower 1>>
            Your shoulders are shot, and each swing feels heavier than the last. The hammer nearly slips from your grip, and you have to take a moment to adjust. You keep going, but your swings are getting weaker.
            <br><br>
            Riley crosses their arms. "Grit your damn teeth and finish."
        <<else>><<willpower 2>>
            Your body gives out before your mind. The hammer slips from your grasp, crashing onto the floor. You bend over, gasping, trying to lift it again, but your arms refuse to obey.
            <br><br>
            Riley sighs, shaking their head. "Weak grip, weak mind."
        <</if>>
        <br><br>

        Riley cracks their knuckles. "That's  15 minutes down. Next station. Don't waste my time."
    <</addinlineevent>>
    <<runeventpool>>
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Conditioning Lesson 2]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Conditioning Lesson 2
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "mma_gym">><<effects>>
<<tiredness 6>><<wearandtear>><<pass 15>>
<<cleareventpool>>
<<addinlineevent "Medicine Ball Slams">>
    The gym floor is scuffed and worn, a testament to years of punishment. In front of you sits a heavy medicine ball, its surface rough and firm. Riley picks it up and slams it into the ground with a deep thud, the force sending vibrations through the floor.
    <br><br>

    "Fifty slams. Full power. If you let up, I will know."
    <br><br>

    You grab the ball, feeling its weight settle in your hands.
    <<if $physique gte 10000>><<physique 1>><<set _effort to 0>>
        The ball is light in your hands. You lift it overhead and slam it down with a clean, controlled motion, the rebound barely phasing you. Each rep is fast, powerful, effortless.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches but says nothing, only giving a short nod.
    <<elseif $physique gte 6000>><<physique 2>><<set _effort to 1>>
        The first slams feel good, but the weight starts settling in by the halfway mark. Your shoulders burn, core tightens, but you keep moving. Each slam still has force, but it is getting harder to maintain.
        <br><br>
        Riley grunts. "You are feeling it now, aren't you?"
    <<elseif $physique gte 3000>><<physique 3>><<set _effort to 2>>
        The ball feels heavier every rep. Your breath gets uneven, shoulders screaming as you force each slam. The last few reps are pure willpower.
        <br><br>
        Riley exhales. "That struggle means you need more work."
    <<else>><<physique 4>><<set _effort to 3>>
        The ball is a monster in your hands. Every lift feels like a battle, and by the twentieth slam, your arms are barely cooperating. Your grip weakens, body trembling with effort.
        <br><br>
        Riley shakes their head. "You call that a slam? Put some damn force behind it."
    <</if>>
    <br><br>

    Riley does not let up. "No stopping. No weak reps."
    <<if _effort is 0 or $willpower gte 600>><<willpower 0.25>>
        Your body falls into rhythm. The weight is there, but your mind blocks it out. Each slam is as strong as the first, your breathing controlled.
        <br><br>
        Riley smirks. "Good. That is the focus you need."
    <<elseif _effort is 1 or $willpower gte 400>><<willpower 0.5>>
        Your muscles burn, but you grit your teeth and keep slamming. The ball feels heavier, but you refuse to slow down.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches. "That is how you build grit."
    <<elseif _effort is 2 or $willpower gte 200>><<willpower 1>>
        Your pace starts breaking down. Each slam gets weaker, shoulders barely holding on. You manage to finish, but your arms are dead weight.
        <br><br>
        Riley crosses their arms. "You better get stronger fast."
    <<else>><<willpower 2>>
        Your arms fail completely before the last ten reps. The ball slips from your grip, and you drop to your knees, panting.
        <br><br>
        Riley shakes their head. "Pathetic. You better not give me a repeat performance next time."
    <</if>>
    <br><br>

    Riley checks the time. "That is 15 minutes. Next station. Do not waste my time."
<</addinlineevent>>
<<addinlineevent "Jump Rope">>
    The rhythmic slap of jump ropes fills the gym, a constant beat of movement and focus. Riley tosses you a rope, the handles wrapped in faded grip tape.
    <br><br>

    "Ten minutes. No tripping, no stopping. Keep the pace up," Riley says, arms crossed.
    <br><br>

    You grip the handles and start skipping.
    <<if $physique gte 10000>><<physique 0.25>><<athletics 2>><<set _effort to 0>>
        Your movements are smooth and effortless. The rope spins without a hitch, feet barely touching the ground as you keep a perfect rhythm.
        <br><br>
        Riley gives a short nod. "Good. Now speed it up."
    <<elseif $physique gte 6000>><<physique 0.5>><<athletics 4>><<set _effort to 1>>
        You find a steady pace, but the burn kicks in early. Your calves tighten, shoulders start to ache, but you push through, keeping the rope moving.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches with an unreadable expression. "Keep your form. Do not get sloppy."
    <<elseif $physique gte 3000>><<physique 1>><<athletics 6>><<set _effort to 2>>
        The rope keeps clipping your toes, breaking your momentum. Every restart makes your breathing more uneven, sweat already trickling down your back.
        <br><br>
        Riley exhales sharply. "You planning on tripping all day, or are you gonna get it together?"
    <<else>><<physique 2>><<athletics 8>><<set _effort to 3>>
        You barely last a minute before your legs start giving out. The rope whips against your shins as you fumble through each jump. Your breathing is ragged, muscles burning from the constant mistakes.
        <br><br>
        Riley sighs. "Pathetic. Get your feet under you and try again."
    <</if>>
    <br><br>

    As the minutes pass, endurance becomes the real test.
    <br><br>

    Riley does not let up. "Do not stop. Keep moving."
    <<if _effort is 0 or $willpower gte 600>><<willpower 0.25>>
        Your body falls into a rhythm, breathing steady. You push past the burn, focusing only on the beat of the rope and your footwork.
        <br><br>
        Riley gives a rare smirk. "Not bad. Now keep that pace next time you are under pressure."
    <<elseif _effort is 1 or $willpower gte 400>><<willpower 0.5>>
        Your lungs burn, legs feel heavy, but you refuse to slow down. Each jump is a battle, but you force your way through.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches. "Hurts? Good. That means you are getting somewhere."
    <<elseif _effort is 2 or $willpower gte 200>><<willpower 1>>
        Your movements get sluggish. Every few jumps, the rope catches, breaking your pace. You keep going, but your form is falling apart.
        <br><br>
        Riley shakes their head. "Fix that footwork. You are not gonna last in a real fight moving like that."
    <<else>><<willpower 2>>
        Your legs give out before the timer hits zero. The rope slips from your hands, and you collapse onto your knees, gasping for air.
        <br><br>
        Riley scoffs. "Weak legs, weak lungs. You better fix both."
    <</if>>
    <br><br>

    Riley checks the time. "That is ten minutes. Next station. Do not waste my time."
<</addinlineevent>>
<<addinlineevent "Shuttle Runs">>
    The gym floor is marked with faded lines, a reminder of countless drills before you. Riley stands at one end, arms crossed, a stopwatch in hand.
    <br><br>

    "Sprint to the line, touch the ground, sprint back. No slowing down, no breaks. 15 minutes."
    <br><br>

    You take your stance, weight shifted forward, ready to push off.
    <<if $physique gte 10000>><<physique 0.25>><<athletics 2>><<set _effort to 0>>
        Your movements are sharp and controlled. Each sprint is explosive, feet pounding against the floor with precision. Your breathing stays steady, your turns crisp.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches, unimpressed but not correcting you. "That is how it is done. Keep that speed up."
    <<elseif $physique gte 6000>><<physique 0.5>><<athletics 4>><<set _effort to 1>>
        The first few runs feel good, but the burn creeps in fast. Your legs start feeling heavier, turns get sloppier, but you grit your teeth and keep going.
        <br><br>
        Riley grunts. "You slowing down already?"
    <<elseif $physique gte 3000>><<physique 1>><<athletics 6>><<set _effort to 2>>
        The quick turns and bursts of speed wear you down fast. By the fifth round, your lungs burn, your legs feel like lead, and your pace is starting to lag.
        <br><br>
        Riley exhales sharply. "If that is your top speed, you better start running faster."
    <<else>><<physique 2>><<athletics 8>><<set _effort to 3>>
        Your legs buckle after only a few sprints. The rapid direction changes are killing your endurance, and every turn feels like dragging dead weight across the floor.
        <br><br>
        Riley shakes their head. "That ain't a sprint. That is a damn jog. Move your feet."
    <</if>>
    <br><br>

    The timer keeps ticking. The real battle now is endurance.
    <br><br>

    Riley does not let up. "No walking. No excuses. Keep going."
    <<if _effort is 0 or $willpower gte 600>><<willpower 0.25>>
        Your legs burn, but your mind is locked in. You force your body to keep the pace, refusing to slow down.
        <br><br>
        Riley smirks. "That is how you push past the pain."
    <<elseif _effort is 1 or $willpower gte 400>><<willpower 0.5>>
        Your form starts slipping, turns getting wider, sprints losing power. But you fight through it, lungs screaming, muscles begging for a break.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches. "That is what I want to see. Now do not quit."
    <<elseif _effort is 2 or $willpower gte 200>><<willpower 1>>
        Your speed drops hard. Every sprint feels like a struggle, every turn a risk of collapsing. You are barely hanging on.
        <br><br>
        Riley crosses their arms. "If this was a fight, you would be dead already."
    <<else>><<willpower 2>>
        You break. Your steps turn into a slow, stumbling jog. Your vision swims, body running on fumes. By the last few sprints, you are barely moving.
        <br><br>
        Riley sighs. "That was embarrassing. Work on your stamina."
    <</if>>
    <br><br>

    Riley checks the time. "That is 15 minutes. Next station. Do not waste my time."
<</addinlineevent>>
<<runeventpool>>
<br><br>

