:: Conditioning Lesson 3
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "mma_gym">><<effects>>
<<tiredness 6>><<wearandtear>><<pass 15>>
<<cleareventpool>>
<<addinlineevent "Hanging Leg Raises">>
    The pull-up bar stands firm, the metal cold under your grip. Riley gestures to it with a nod.
    <br><br>

    "Hang from the bar. Knees to chest. No swinging. 15 minutes."
    <br><br>

    You jump up, gripping tight as your body settles into position.
    <<if $physique gte 10000>><<physique 1>><<set _effort to 0>>
        Your abs contract with minimal effort. Each lift is smooth and controlled, knees rising to your chest with precision. Your grip holds firm, body staying completely stable.
        <br><br>
        Riley gives a rare nod. "That is how it should look."
    <<elseif $physique gte 6000>><<physique 2>><<set _effort to 1>>
        The first few reps feel fine, but your grip starts wearing out. Your core stays engaged, but by the halfway mark, your arms begin trembling from holding yourself up.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches. "You better not drop before the timer is up."
    <<elseif $physique gte 3000>><<physique 3>><<set _effort to 2>>
        The weight of your own body starts working against you. Your knees do not reach as high anymore, and your grip weakens fast. Every rep takes more effort to control.
        <br><br>
        Riley exhales sharply. "You are gonna need a stronger core if you plan on lasting in the ring."
    <<else>><<physique 4>><<set _effort to 3>>
        The first few reps feel impossible. Your arms burn instantly, grip slipping as your body swings uncontrollably. You barely manage to lift your knees halfway before they drop like dead weight.
        <br><br>
        Riley shakes their head. "That is embarrassing. You better start training that core seriously."
    <</if>>
    <br><br>

    The real fight is against fatigue.
    <br><br>

    Riley does not let up. "Do not drop. Hold on."
    <<if _effort is 0 or $willpower gte 600>><<willpower 0.25>>
        Your focus stays sharp. The burn is there, but you lock it out, refusing to let go.
        <br><br>
        Riley nods slightly. "That is real endurance."
    <<elseif _effort is 1 or $willpower gte 400>><<willpower 0.5>>
        Your arms shake violently, core screaming, but you fight through it, keeping yourself up with sheer willpower.
        <br><br>
        Riley smirks. "Pain means it is working."
    <<elseif _effort is 2 or $willpower gte 200>><<willpower 1>>
        You can barely hold on. The last few reps are sloppy, your legs barely moving. Your body fights against you, and you are seconds away from falling.
        <br><br>
        Riley crosses their arms. "If that is all you have got, you better fix it."
    <<else>><<willpower 2>>
        Your grip fails completely. Your hands slip, and you drop to the floor, gasping, arms limp at your sides.
        <br><br>
        Riley scoffs. "Weak grip, weak core. Fix it."
    <</if>>
    <br><br>

    Riley checks the time. "That is 15 minutes. Next station. Do not waste my time."
<</addinlineevent>>
<<addinlineevent "Plank with Shoulder Taps">>
    The gym mat beneath you is rough, worn down from years of training. Riley stands over you, arms crossed.
    <br><br>

    "Hold the plank. Tap your shoulder every five seconds. If your hips drop, you start over."
    <br><br>

    You drop into position, balancing on your forearms and toes.
    <<if $physique gte 10000>><<physique 1>><<set _effort to 0>>
        Your core is solid like a rock. Each shoulder tap is precise, and your body remains completely still, no wasted movement.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches but does not comment. "That is how it should look."
    <<elseif $physique gte 6000>><<physique 2>><<set _effort to 1>>
        Your arms start shaking early, but you lock your core in place. Every tap feels like a test of control, but you hold strong.
        <br><br>
        Riley gives a short nod. "Keep that back straight."
    <<elseif $physique gte 3000>><<physique 3>><<set _effort to 2>>
        Your hips start sagging halfway through. Every tap throws off your balance, forcing you to adjust constantly. Sweat drips from your forehead.
        <br><br>
        Riley exhales sharply. "Get your body under control."
    <<else>><<physique 4>><<set _effort to 3>>
        You collapse barely a minute in. Every tap knocks you off balance, and your core is not strong enough to stabilize.
        <br><br>
        Riley shakes their head. "That is embarrassing. Get up."
    <</if>>
    <br><br>

    The real test is mental.
    <br><br>

    Riley does not let up. "Hold that plank. Do not drop."
    <<if _effort is 0 or $willpower gte 600>><<willpower 0.25>>
        You breathe steady, muscles locked in place. Your body wants to shake, but you refuse to let it.
        <br><br>
        Riley smirks. "Good control."
    <<elseif _effort is 1 or $willpower gte 400>><<willpower 0.5>>
        Your arms burn, balance wavers, but you grit your teeth and fight through it.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches. "Pain is part of the deal."
    <<elseif _effort is 2 or $willpower gte 200>><<willpower 1>>
        Your hips keep sagging, every second feeling longer than the last. You barely hold on.
        <br><br>
        Riley crosses their arms. "You better not drop now."
    <<else>><<willpower 2>>
        You collapse to the mat, arms giving out, chest heaving.
        <br><br>
        Riley scoffs. "You got work to do."
    <</if>>
    <br><br>

    Riley checks the time. "That is 15 minutes. Next station. Do not waste my time."
<</addinlineevent>>
<<addinlineevent "Russian Twists">>
    The weight of the medicine ball settles into your hands as you sit on the gym floor, feet slightly raised. Riley kneels beside you, watching closely.
    <br><br>

    "Twist side to side. Ball touches the floor each time. No half-reps. 15 minutes."
    <br><br>

    You lock in your posture, tightening your core as you start the motion.  
    <<if $physique gte 10000>><<physique 1>><<set _effort to 0>>
        Each twist is sharp and controlled. Your core engages without struggle, the weight nothing more than a tool in your hands. No wasted movement, no signs of fatigue.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches. "Solid. Now keep it that way."
    <<elseif $physique gte 6000>><<physique 2>><<set _effort to 1>>
        The first few reps are steady, but as time drags on, your core starts burning. The weight feels heavier, and the twists take more effort.
        <br><br>
        Riley grunts. "You feeling it? Good. That means it is working."
    <<elseif $physique gte 3000>><<physique 3>><<set _effort to 2>>
        Your twists start losing form. Your back arches slightly, shoulders tense up, and each rep feels heavier than the last.
        <br><br>
        Riley exhales sharply. "Keep your back straight. You do not slack on this."
    <<else>><<physique 4>><<set _effort to 3>>
        The ball wobbles in your grip. Your core fails early, twists turning into weak shuffles rather than full movements.
        <br><br>
        Riley shakes their head. "That ain't a twist. That is just struggling."
    <</if>>
    <br><br>

    The real fight is against fatigue.
    <br><br>

    Riley does not let up. "No stopping. Keep twisting."
    <<if _effort is 0 or $willpower gte 600>><<willpower 0.25>>
        Your breathing stays steady, the burn creeping in, but you stay locked in. Each twist lands clean, pace unchanged.
        <br><br>
        Riley smirks. "That is the focus you need."
    <<elseif _effort is 1 or $willpower gte 400>><<willpower 0.5>>
        Your grip tightens, shoulders aching, but you push through. The weight slows you down, but you refuse to stop.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches. "That is how you build grit."
    <<elseif _effort is 2 or $willpower gte 200>><<willpower 1>>
        Your pace breaks down. Each twist takes effort just to stay balanced. Your arms and core scream for a break.
        <br><br>
        Riley crosses their arms. "You better get stronger fast."
    <<else>><<willpower 2>>
        Your arms give out before the last ten reps. The ball slips from your grip, and you drop to the mat, gasping.
        <br><br>
        Riley scoffs. "Pathetic. You better not give me a repeat performance next time."
    <</if>>
    <br><br>

    Riley checks the time. "That is 15 minutes. Next station. Do not waste my time."
<</addinlineevent>>
