:: Conditioning Lesson 4
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "mma_gym">><<effects>>
<<tiredness 6>><<wearandtear>><<pass 15>>
<<cleareventpool>>
<<addinlineevent "Controlled Breathing Under Stress">>
    The air in the gym is thick with heat and exertion. Riley tosses you onto the mat, motioning for you to lie flat.
    <br><br>

    "You are gonna push your body past the edge, and then you are gonna get it back under control. Burpees, non-stop. When I say stop, you drop and focus on your breathing. If you cannot bring your heart rate down fast enough, we go again. 15 minutes."
    <br><br>

    Your legs already feel heavy as you start. The drill begins.  
    <<if $athletics gte 600>><<athletics 2>><<set _effort to 0>>
        You move through the burpees without hesitation, body responding like a machine. When Riley calls for stillness, you drop, breathing slow and steady, your recovery almost instant.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches. "Good control. Now keep it."  
    <<elseif $athletics gte 400>><<athletics 4>><<set _effort to 1>>
        The first set is fine, but your lungs burn by the second. When you drop, your chest heaves, but you fight to calm it down.
        <br><br>
        Riley grunts. "That is not bad. But not good enough."  
    <<elseif $athletics gte 200>><<athletics 6>><<set _effort to 2>>
        You struggle to keep pace by the second round. Every jump feels heavier, and when you stop, your heart slams against your ribs, breath completely out of sync.
        <br><br>
        Riley exhales. "You are panicking. Fix it."  
    <<else>><<athletics 8>><<set _effort to 3>>
        You barely make it past the first round. Every muscle in your body screams in protest, and when you stop, you cannot get your breath under control. Your chest rises and falls uncontrollably.
        <br><br>
        Riley shakes their head. "You are a mess. Again."  
    <</if>>  
    <br><br>

    The real test is mental. Mastering control under exhaustion.
    <br><br>

    Riley does not let up. "Control it. Slow it down."
    <br><br>

    <<if _effort is 0 or $willpower gte 600>><<willpower 1>>
        Your mind blocks out the chaos. Each breath is intentional, heart rate lowering within seconds. You regain control before Riley can call for another round.
        <br><br>
        Riley smirks. "That is how you handle pressure."  
    <<elseif _effort is 1 or $willpower gte 400>><<willpower 2>>
        It takes effort, but you force your breath to slow, even though your body still wants to panic.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches. "Not bad. But you should not have to fight for it."  
    <<elseif _effort is 2 or $willpower gte 200>><<willpower 4>>
        Your breath is ragged, and even as you try to control it, your heart is still pounding. It takes too long to stabilize, and Riley shakes their head.
        <br><br>
        "If you cannot control yourself, how do you expect to control a fight?"  
    <<else>><<willpower 8>>
        You cannot slow down. Your lungs refuse to listen, breath coming in short, desperate gasps. Your body is in full panic mode.
        <br><br>
        Riley sighs. "You better learn fast, or you will not last a second under pressure."  
    <</if>>  
    <br><br>

    Riley checks the time. "That is 15 minutes. Next station. Do not waste my time."  
<</addinlineevent>>
<<addinlineevent "Wall Sit Challenge">>
    The concrete wall behind you is cold against your back. Riley stands nearby, arms crossed, watching.
    <br><br>

    "Drop into position. Knees at ninety degrees. Hold it. No breaks, no leaning forward. 15 minutes."
    <br><br>

    You lower yourself down, thighs already tensing.  
    <<if $physique gte 10000>><<physique 1>><<set _effort to 0>>
        The burn comes, but it is nothing you cannot handle. You stay locked in, breathing steady, muscles holding firm.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches but says nothing.  
    <<elseif $physique gte 6000>><<physique 2>><<set _effort to 1>>
        The first few minutes are fine, but your thighs start screaming. Sweat drips down your back as you force yourself to stay still.
        <br><br>
        Riley nods. "Now we see who actually has discipline."  
    <<elseif $physique gte 3000>><<physique 3>><<set _effort to 2>>
        Your legs start shaking early. Every second feels longer than the last, and your back burns against the wall.
        <br><br>
        Riley exhales. "You are breaking already? Fix that."  
    <<else>><<physique 4>><<set _effort to 3>>
        You barely last a minute. Your thighs give out fast, body sliding down against your will.
        <br><br>
        Riley shakes their head. "That is weak. Get back up."  
    <</if>>  
    <br><br>

    The challenge is not just pain—it is staying still when everything in your body tells you to quit.
    <br><br>

    Riley does not let up. "No shaking. Hold it."
    <br><br>

    <<if _effort is 0 or $willpower gte 600>><<willpower 1>>
        Your body wants to collapse, but you refuse. You hold still, breathing through the pain, eyes locked forward.
        <br><br>
        Riley smirks. "That is the mental strength I want to see."  
    <<elseif _effort is 1 or $willpower gte 400>><<willpower 2>>
        Your legs are trembling, breath shaky, but you hold on. Barely. Every second feels like an eternity.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches. "Good. But you should not look that miserable yet."  
    <<elseif _effort is 2 or $willpower gte 200>><<willpower 4>>
        Your thighs scream, body begging to drop. You hold on, but your willpower is the only thing keeping you up.
        <br><br>
        Riley crosses their arms. "You are on the edge. Do not break now."  
    <<else>><<willpower 8>>
        Your legs fail completely. Your back slides down the wall, knees buckling, chest heaving.
        <br><br>
        Riley sighs. "Pathetic. You better get tougher, fast."  
    <</if>>  
    <br><br>

    Riley checks the time. "That is 15 minutes. Next station. Do not waste my time."  
<</addinlineevent>>
<<addinlineevent "Cold Showers and Ice Baths">>
    The locker room is quiet except for the distant sounds of the gym. The cold tub sits waiting, ice floating on the surface. Riley stands beside it, arms crossed.
    <br><br>

    "15 minutes. No flinching, no whining. You break early, we go again."
    <br><br>

    You take a deep breath and step forward.  
    <<if $willpower gte 800>><<willpower 2>><<set _effort to 0>>
        The cold hits like a shock, but you barely react. Your breathing stays controlled, muscles locked in place. The ice water might as well be room temperature.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches. "No reaction. Good. You actually have discipline."  
    <<elseif $willpower gte 6000>><<willpower 3>><<set _effort to 1>>
        The moment you step in, your body tenses, breath catching for a second. It takes effort, but you force yourself to stay still, focus on the pain, and control it.
        <br><br>
        Riley grunts. "I see you are feeling it. Keep it together."  
    <<elseif $willpower gte 3000>><<willpower 4>><<set _effort to 2>>
        The cold cuts through your skin instantly. Your body locks up, breath coming in short, ragged gasps as you fight the instinct to pull away.
        <br><br>
        Riley exhales. "You are panicking. Slow it down."  
    <<else>><<willpower 5>><<set _effort to 3>>
        The cold is unbearable. The moment it touches your skin, your lungs seize up, and your muscles cramp. You try to stay in, but your body thrashes involuntarily.
        <br><br>
        Riley shakes their head. "That ain't control. That is panic."  
    <</if>>  
    <br><br>

    The minutes drag on. The fight is against yourself.
    <br><br>

    Riley does not let up. "If you cannot handle a little discomfort, you will never handle real pain."
    <br><br>

    <<if _effort is 0 or $willpower gte 600>><<willpower 2>>
        Your mind blocks out the cold. Every second in the ice becomes just another test of control. Your breathing stays steady, and you refuse to shiver.
        <br><br>
        Riley smirks. "Now that is discipline."  
    <<elseif _effort is 1 or $willpower gte 400>><<willpower 3>>
        Your limbs shake, teeth clenching, but you refuse to move. The pain is there, but you fight it, controlling each breath with sheer will.
        <br><br>
        Riley watches. "Not bad. But you should not have to fight for it this hard."  
    <<elseif _effort is 2 or $willpower gte 200>><<willpower 4>>
        Your body is barely cooperating. Every second feels like an hour, every breath a struggle against the ice. You are moments away from breaking.
        <br><br>
        Riley crosses their arms. "You are close to quitting. Hold on."  
    <<else>><<willpower 5>>
        You snap. The pain becomes too much, and you jerk out of the water, gasping, limbs numb and trembling uncontrollably.
        <br><br>
        Riley exhales. "Weak mind, weak body. If you cannot handle this, you are done before the fight even starts."  
    <</if>>  
    <br><br>

    Riley checks the time. "That is 15 minutes. Next station. Do not waste my time."  
